<title>HONG KONG: China Southern gets 1st of 10 Airbus 320s.</title>
<headline>China Southern gets 1st of 10 Airbus 320s.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Guangzhou-based China Southern Airlines has taken delivery of the first of 10 Airbus A320 aircraft to be delivered this year, according to a statement from Airbus Industrie.</p>
<p>China's largest airline in terms of passengers carried has 20 A320s powered by International Aero Engines V2500 engines on firm order, the statement added.</p>
<p>Tong Keisheng, the airline's chief economist, said the decision to acquire the A320 was based on a competitive evaluation of all 160-seat aircraft on the market.</p>
<p>&quot;The A320 is the most advanced and therefore the best choice,&quot; he said in the statement.</p>
